{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/842225-conscription-national-service-jury-duty-and-other-annoying-legal-obligations","id":842225,"title":"Conscription, National service, Jury duty, and other annoying legal obligations.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-04T16:27:48-08:00","id":842225,"title":"Conscription, National service, Jury duty, and other annoying legal obligations.","content":"how do you think supernaturals offset such things, I could see some of the SAD's investigations starting with mysterious draft dodging cases with people either disappearing, or getting disqualifed under mysterious circumstances...<br /> <br /> vampires pretty much HAVE to have a way around such things because of problems with sunlight<br /> <br /> Garou will probaly try to evade conscription unless they suspect something wyrmish behind enemy lines, <br /> <br /> They would probaly in most cases accept jury duty, unless they were URGENTLY needed by the local sept. (I could see pentex arranging a jury summons for a known garou, just to tie them up) as it lets them see how the Wyrm has affected the city they live in...<br /> <br /> Wraiths, its a nonissue, by and large.<br /> <br /> Ideas on others?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:19:37-08:00","id":842263,"title":"","content":"Which country are we talking about? Conscription is technically on the books in some countries but hasn't been used in decades, while in other countries is an assumed fact of teenage life.<br /> <br /> That said, pretty much every country that has mandatory service in some form, as long since learned how to deal with individuals that shouldn't/can't be doing it.<br /> <br /> 1) A lot of supernaturals take themselves off the grid, or were never on it. Lupus and Metis Garou, for example, might not have official papers, which means nobody is coming after them to serve in these things. A vampire that's 100 years old has already figured out either how to remove themselves from the system, or create new identities in the system which can be crafted to avoid service.<br /> <br /> 2) In countries with universal conscription, there's pretty much always options for avowed pacifists, people with mental disorders, and people with significant medical issues. I have some in-laws in Israel. One of them didn't go into military service because they got recruited by one of Israel's intelligence services to work as an analyst instead. Another did a four year degree program followed by a graduate research project in agricultural studies (which the Israeli government is all for because high levels of STEM industry is important to their economy, and agricultural independence is important to their concept of national security). Another was exempted completely because of a serious spinal injury when they were younger.<br /> <br /> 3) Government generally really don't want to deal with actively unwilling individuals. One of the reasons things like jury pools are as large as they are, is because they know some percentage of people will do everything to get out of it; and most of them that don't want to serve jury duty will manage to get out of it. Trying to use jury duty to pull Garou away from a Sept would be pointless. All of them just need to call up and say, &quot;Hey, this date? It sucks for me, [insert one of dozens reasonable excuses], can we reschedule?&quot; Because the universal response from jury selectors is of course you can reschedule.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:25:42-08:00","id":842272,"title":"","content":"Funny story, the previous owner of my house is dead yet I still receive a summons for him from time to time. Good old USA bureaucracy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T04:02:16-08:00","id":842476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/842225-conscription-national-service-jury-duty-and-other-annoying-legal-obligations#post842225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">h<br /> They would probaly in most cases accept jury duty, unless they were URGENTLY needed by the local sept. (I could see pentex arranging a jury summons for a known garou, just to tie them up) as it lets them see how the Wyrm has affected the city they live in...</div> </div> </div> </div>If Pentex knew their names, residences, social security numbers and all that other lovely stuff, Jury duty would be the least of Garou's problems.<br /> <br /> And for instance, where I live - there is no jury duty and military service is optional. Practically all my commitments to the government can be sorted by paying a bill and going to an office to get paperwork once in a blue moon. That's even been made better by the recent introduction of digital paperwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 03-05-2016, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T06:07:38-08:00","id":842508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/842225-conscription-national-service-jury-duty-and-other-annoying-legal-obligations?p=842272#post842272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny story, the previous owner of my house is dead yet I still receive a summons for him from time to time. Good old USA bureaucracy</div> </div> </div> </div> Had 2 cases where Police officers arrrived at my door looking for the previous tennant of my apartment. I can only guess he was either under witness protection or a felon. possibly he moved without leaving a forwarding address...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T17:32:17-08:00","id":842799,"title":"","content":"This is why supernatural beings really need to go &quot;off the grid&quot; or pay their dues to other creatures of their kind who have Influence.<br /> <br /> For Vampire, this can be easy. Pay your boons to the elders, probably Ventrue, who can put a stop to it using their Influence. There is a reason they are in charge, and getting mortal authorities to not be interested in you is one reason the other clans want them in charge.<br /> <br /> For Werewolf, this should be easy. The game assumes most Garou are runaways who flee into the woods. They don't leave forwarding addresses. For most Garou this solves the problem. There is probably a minority who still have a real identity and paperwork trail in the world of the Flock, and they can be issues. However, sufficient Gifts and favors done to Glass Walkers (and sometimes others) can probably reduce the nuisance value.<br /> <br /> For Mage, this shouldn't be much of an issue. It can be handled case by case. Some Mages can just eat this and move on. It's not like they can't handle it unlike the previous two. Others can handle it with Arcane or appropriate magic.<br /> <br /> For Wraith, this is a non issue. But they have to put up with their equivalents for real under the Hierarchy.<br /> <br /> For Changeling, it depends. Most Changelings are either under the age of this kind of thing, moved completely into the Dreaming with few ties to the mundane world, or are recognized as being mentally ill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T09:14:18-08:00","id":843011,"title":"","content":"A vampire is going to have to fake their deaths at some point, because of no aging if nothing else. Fortunately, vampires are rich and well connected so I assume that getting a child's off the the grid is one of the parts of being a sire. <br /> <br /> For other WoD creatures, getting out of the system is more optional, though it would probably be bad for a werewolf to be under too much government scrutiny. Maybe fake ID's and such are one way that Glass Walkers make themselves useful for other werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T18:43:14-08:00","id":844261,"title":"","content":"Jury Duty might provide another reason why having a Tzimisce or two in the Camarilla is handy: pay them to craft a ghoul to your likeness, and have them show up to Jury Duty. It would certainly be useful for Kindred who don't want to kill off their old lives, like with famous or infamous public figures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T10:00:25-08:00","id":844572,"title":"","content":"Oh curious, that reminds me, once a discipline is taught out of clan can it Do you favor letting the leak spread? how far can obternatioin go from one lasombra antitribu?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T13:00:26-08:00","id":844684,"title":"","content":"By the rules, once you know a Discipline, you can teach it. Any controls would be social, not metaphyiscal, in nature. Which is why a lot of Clans are protective about their special Disciplines, and will probably try to arrange for the final Death of both Clanmates that get instruction happy, and their pupils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T17:19:30-08:00","id":844814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/842225-conscription-national-service-jury-duty-and-other-annoying-legal-obligations?p=844684#post844684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the rules, once you know a Discipline, you can teach it. Any controls would be social, not metaphyiscal, in nature. Which is why a lot of Clans are protective about their special Disciplines, and will probably try to arrange for the final Death of both Clanmates that get instruction happy, and their pupils.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Disciplines are also &quot;spooky&quot; even by Kindred reckoning, or are known by spooky Clans. Obtenebration, for instance, is frightening in its unnaturalness, to a degree most Disciplines aren't. Quietus, meanwhile, is the signature skill set of the Assamites, largely known for being ruthless assassins and diablerists. In either case, a Kindred's reputation could suffer greatly if they are known to possess a particular Discipline, either because some Kindred see the power as practically demonic, or because it implies a connection to unsavory Cainites. Or it could lead folks to suspect that you might BE of one of those Clans, and have been lying about your identity the whole time. A Kindred found with Vicissitude is virtually guaranteed to be decried as a Tzimisce in disguise, on top of being seen as truly alien and horrifying just for having the power.<br /> <br /> This, incidentally, is a mark in the Sabbat's favor. They share blood, resources, and knowledge freely with each other, and have plenty of Cainites from most Clans and bloodlines attached to them. It's common for them to teach each other Disciplines. Granted, some Lasombra and Tzimisce are likely wary of teaching their respective signatures. But there are also plenty of young licks who give not a rat's ass about their Clan's history or whatever, and share them freely with their pack-mates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T22:14:08-08:00","id":844926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/842225-conscription-national-service-jury-duty-and-other-annoying-legal-obligations?p=844572#post844572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh curious, that reminds me, once a discipline is taught out of clan can it Do you favor letting the leak spread? how far can obternatioin go from one lasombra antitribu?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly certain the clan as a whole takes a dim view of such teachings and the offending teacher would probably find their name dropped rather quickly in the court of shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T08:05:05-08:00","id":845083,"title":"","content":"Fair points, Oh on Thaumatalagy or Necromancy, Once I've learned one of them, can I Research new paths on my own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T08:30:06-08:00","id":845096,"title":"","content":"I think it would be the most effective as a storytelling tool in a Hunter game, since a big aspect of that is balancing normal life with the Hunt. Especially if there's say, a ghouled lawyer or judge involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T16:56:07-08:00","id":845352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/842225-conscription-national-service-jury-duty-and-other-annoying-legal-obligations?p=845083#post845083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair points, Oh on Thaumatalagy or Necromancy, Once I've learned one of them, can I Research new paths on my own?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can but it can be a pain to explain how you do it to your St if your PC doesn't have resources to facilitate said research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T18:15:10-08:00","id":845380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/842225-conscription-national-service-jury-duty-and-other-annoying-legal-obligations?p=844684#post844684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the rules, once you know a Discipline, you can teach it. Any controls would be social, not metaphyiscal, in nature. Which is why a lot of Clans are protective about their special Disciplines, and will probably try to arrange for the final Death of both Clanmates that get instruction happy, and their pupils.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than the Tremere regarding Hermetic Thaumaturgy, I've not gotten the impression that clans are overly concerned as a whole about their signature disciplines making it out into general population. It's probably not nearly as common as trading instruction in the more mainstream disciplines, but there aren't death squads running around punishing anyone who teaches Chimeristry or Serpentis to an outsider on behalf of some micromanaging clan-wide organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T00:57:22-08:00","id":845512,"title":"","content":"Depends a bit on the era, and Sect. And you seem to be exaggerating my intent there. There's a difference between a tolerance for there to be some outsiders that learn the Discipline, and smacking down those that aren't careful with it. The Assamites aren't going to worry about a relatively trusted ally learning Quietus. But they're going to find out if a domain is full of non-Assamites running around with it, and not going to be happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T16:39:14-08:00","id":846328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/842225-conscription-national-service-jury-duty-and-other-annoying-legal-obligations?p=844926#post844926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fairly certain the clan as a whole takes a dim view of such teachings and the offending teacher would probably find their name dropped rather quickly in the court of shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any more so then with Lasombra antitribu in general? <br /> <br /> Though I think even most Lasombra Antitribu will probaly sell their Signature Discipline DEARLY knowing once its taught its, taught, and you cant control where it goes from there, and offering it to interested Cainites is a good bargaining tool, but GIVE it away, and its power as a negotiating tool disappears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T17:56:23-08:00","id":846352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/842225-conscription-national-service-jury-duty-and-other-annoying-legal-obligations?p=846328#post846328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a>