omain or chantry, how do I handle my Tax paperwork to keep from getting in trouble, this is probaly another thing you'd have ghouls and kind devoted to. Wanted to ask, what traits do Fences Need other then Streetwise, figure the garou have a number of Fences amongst their Kinfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T11:20:28-07:00","id":850202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/842225-conscription-national-service-jury-duty-and-other-annoying-legal-obligations?p=850193#post850193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh something barely Related? Taxes, if I'm an alchemist, got money from my sept, the domain or chantry, how do I handle my Tax paperwork to keep from getting in trouble, this is probaly another thing you'd have ghouls and kind devoted to. Wanted to ask, what traits do Fences Need other then Streetwise, figure the garou have a number of Fences amongst their Kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, because you totally have to report all that lead to gold you made......\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T13:46:03-07:00","id":850240,"title":"","content":"I KNOW you dont but was asking if your using it in any way that will be visible... You want to make sure you have a legitimate papertrail, do you try forging it into jewelry then sale that, or whatTo avoid (If you let it be visible in your living standard) Being charged with tax evasion, or someone suspecting your &quot;Living beyond your appearent means&quot; And thus must be a crook...<br /> <br /> Damn never thought to ask that about those who are crooks... might be over analyzing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T14:18:50-07:00","id":850254,"title":"","content":"If you want to deal in such things? Have a business (probably ghoul/etc. run) that handles both auction/reclamation efforts (think things like Storage Wars or any of the number of similar reality TV shows) and deals in resale as a pawn shop.<br /> <br /> The paper trail is pretty much set for you. Report anything like magically created gold as a &quot;find&quot; in an auctioned house/storage unit/etc. that you discovered while picking it apart. Just focus on things (precious metals are actually a boon here) that are incredibly hard/impossible to non-magically trace. You found a bunch of old gold? Well, smelt it down and cast it into bars. Boom. Nobody can prove it wasn't a bunch of jewelry you found in a locker.<br /> <br /> Such businesses also deal with very uneven money flows. A good one will have a stable low level income that covers the basics, but the auction side of it could be a bust for 2-3 months, and then find $100K worth of stuff in a day. So you don't really have to worry about &quot;living beyond your means,&quot; since you can always claim anything that's a sign of wealth was just a lucky find and you felt like keeping it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T15:52:50-07:00","id":850291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/842225-conscription-national-service-jury-duty-and-other-annoying-legal-obligations?p=850254#post850254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to deal in such things? Have a business (probably ghoul/etc. run) that handles both auction/reclamation efforts (think things like Storage Wars or any of the number of similar reality TV shows) and deals in resale as a pawn shop.<br /> <br /> The paper trail is pretty much set for you. Report anything like magically created gold as a &quot;find&quot; in an auctioned house/storage unit/etc. that you discovered while picking it apart. Just focus on things (precious metals are actually a boon here) that are incredibly hard/impossible to non-magically trace. You found a bunch of old gold? Well, smelt it down and cast it into bars. Boom. Nobody can prove it wasn't a bunch of jewelry you found in a locker.<br /> <br /> Such businesses also deal with very uneven money flows. A good one will have a stable low level income that covers the basics, but the auction side of it could be a bust for 2-3 months, and then find $100K worth of stuff in a day. So you don't really have to worry about &quot;living beyond your means,&quot; since you can always claim anything that's a sign of wealth was just a lucky find and you felt like keeping it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or claim it as gambling winnings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T16:13:35-07:00","id":850297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/842225-conscription-national-service-jury-duty-and-other-annoying-legal-obligations?p=850291#post850291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or claim it as gambling winnings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, casinos keep track of people who win big in order to spot card counters and cheaters. The governmentalso looks at those lists to catch people trying to dodge taxes by claiming things are lottery/gambling winnings(which ironically the government taxes a lot more, if you win lotto you only get 25% of the winnings as 50-60% is taken by tax and another 25% is taken if you want to be payed up front. Otherwise they pay you that 50% in small checks over time)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"htt